prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: one wide panoramic illustration for an interactive production chain in a French cartoon village management game, Kanab Quest.
Primary request: create an inviting cutaway Breton farm workshop, a single horizontal row of FIVE equally wide workstations on a genuinely transparent background. Landscape canvas, approximately 3:1 aspect ratio. All five stations fully visible at equal scale, aligned on one low continuous cream work floor. Stations read clearly from left to right:
1) cultivation: a tiny open greenhouse with two potted flowering hemp plants, palmate serrated seven-leaflet leaves, simple teal watering can;
2) maturation: a cream drying cupboard with open teal shutters, a few hanging harvested branches and glass storage jars, a small plain hourglass;
3) hand trimming: a warm apricot workbench, pruning scissors resting next to a tray of compact green flower buds;
4) dry sifting: a compact teal and cream mesh sifting tray, a little golden resin powder collected beneath, no industrial chemistry;
5) selling: a cheerful small cream and teal market counter, neatly closed kraft packets, a mechanical balance and a tiny stack of gold game coins.
Style: friendly French-Belgian cartoon village, confident imperfect near-black ink outlines, broad flat cel colours, very restrained printed stipple shadows. Cream paper tones, deep teal, leafy green, warm apricot orange, golden accents. No dark brown masses. Three-quarter front view, low perspective, readable silhouettes, open work areas. Low slate roof fragments over the first two stations only, keep all objects readable. Enough separation between each equal-width bay for HTML controls to identify the five stages below.
This is environmental art, NOT a UI mockup. No people or faces: the app will show its actual employee portraits. No text, letters, numbers, labels, arrows, logos, buttons, frames, surrounding landscape, background rectangle, checkerboard or watermark. Real alpha transparency around the complete irregular silhouette, generous small outer margins. No cut-off objects. No photorealism, 3D, gradients or pixel art.
